From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:22:17 -0500
Subject: fix: a deleted Space's routes go with it; five more ad-click ids

A deleted Space's rules stayed, and the first rule that matches an address
decides, so one naming no Space hid a later one naming a live Space, and the
link opened where the user was. Its place as the Space for links from other
apps stayed too (routing D5; BACKLOG S-162).

The tracking table gains gbraid, wbraid, srsltid, ttclid and li_fat_id
(copy-link L2; BACKLOG S-155).

Why: both were open items that needed no decision.

Removable when: never as behaviour.
